WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.074
Welcome to our training on the Late Shipment Rate, or LSR.

00:00:04.074 --> 00:00:10.000
Today we'll cover what the LSR is and how it affects sellers in the Amazon Store.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.250
Let's start by defining LSR.

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:18.550
LSR measures the percentage of orders where shipment confirmation occurs after the expected ship

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:19.000
date.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.000
You can find the expected ship date in order details.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:29.737
It's important to note that LSR only applies to seller-fulfilled orders, also known as merchant-

00:00:29.737 --> 00:00:31.000
fulfilled, or MFN.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:37.000
To calculate your LSR, your total orders are divided by those that were ship-confirmed late.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:44.143
So if you've had 100 orders in the last 10 days and two of them were shipped after the expected

00:00:44.143 --> 00:00:47.000
ship date, you'll have an LSR of 2%.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:53.000
Sellers must maintain an LSR under 4% to continue selling in the Amazon Store.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:58.000
An LSR over 4% can result in account deactivation.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:05.000
To view your LSR, head to the Performance tab in Seller Central and select Account Health.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:10.000
In the Shipping Performance section, select Late Shipment Rate.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:16.000
On this page, you'll see your LSR calculated for the last 10 and 30 days.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:22.263
It's important to confirm orders by their expected ship dates so your customers can see their order

00:01:22.263 --> 00:01:23.000
status online.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:29.933
Confirming late can lead to negative customer experiences, increased claims, negative feedback and

00:01:29.933 --> 00:01:31.000
customer contacts.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:37.000
If your LSR is in jeopardy, you may be notified and given 30 days to remedy the situation.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:41.000
If you do not take action, you could risk account deactivation.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:47.000
Now let's review some top tips for improving and maintaining your LSR.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:53.000
First, be sure you only list items you're able to ship by or before their expected ship date.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:59.333
Next, work with your carriers to ensure they will be able to pick up your packages and scan them

00:01:59.333 --> 00:02:00.000
on time.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:05.895
Finally, ensure you confirm shipments with valid tracking information as soon as you hand over packages

00:02:05.895 --> 00:02:07.000
to the carrier.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:12.226
It's also possible that your business has grown during your time in the Amazon store to the point

00:02:12.226 --> 00:02:16.000
where you need to hire more staff to stay on top of orders.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:20.000
Create a daily reminder to check for and prepare orders.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:25.000
Making this a part of your daily routine can help you always ship on time.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:31.400
You can also use Amazon's Buy Shipping Services to simplify the shipping process and remove your

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:33.000
need to confirm shipping.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:39.000
To learn more about Amazon Buy Shipping Services, search for Buy Shipping in Seller University.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:45.261
Preparing for increased order volume during key sales periods like the run-up to holiday seasons

00:02:45.261 --> 00:02:48.000
can help you maintain a healthy LSR.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:54.000
Finally, always check your account health dashboard regularly for notifications.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.000
This concludes our training on the late shipment rate.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon store.
